{
  "id": "matched-pairs-t-test",
  "term": "matched-pairs t test",
  "definition": "A matched-pairs t test is a statistical method used when two related scores are compared as pairs, such as the same students’ questionnaire results before and after an educational activity. It tests whether the average difference within those matched pairs is likely to reflect a real change rather than chance.",
